# 3D Cinematic Website & Animation Rules

## 1. Zero-Lag & Smooth Motion Mandate
- The site must never hang, drop frames, or stutter during scroll or interaction.
- Frame loops must use delta-time clamping (`Math.min(delta, 0.05)`) and exponential damping (`1 - Math.exp(-lambda * dt)`) to remain buttery smooth across 60Hz, 120Hz, and 144Hz displays.
- Transitions must be gentle and organic (using easing curves like `[0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]` or GSAP `power3.out`). Never use jarring instant snap-backs or harsh linear motion.
- Off-screen 3D canvases must pause their render loops via `IntersectionObserver` and the Page Visibility API (`document.hidden`).

## 2. WebGL Architecture & Memory Hygiene
- Dynamically import browser-dependent 3D canvas code with SSR disabled (`next/dynamic` with `{ ssr: false }`).
- Semantic page content, headings, SEO tags, navigation, and interactive CTA controls must remain in standard accessible DOM elements outside the WebGL canvas.
- Maintain zero WebGL memory leaks: every `Geometry`, `Material`, and `Texture` must be explicitly disposed of during component unmount.
- Enforce strict DPR limits: cap `devicePixelRatio` at `1.5` on desktop and `1.0–1.2` on mobile to prevent GPU fill-rate exhaustion.
- Single property ownership: GSAP, Motion, and `useFrame` must never mutate the same transform property at the same time.

## 3. Original 3D Character & IP Safeguards
- Use only original, commissioned, or properly licensed assets with verifiable commercial use and modification rights.
- Never reproduce Transformers characters, names, logos, signature silhouettes, or recognizable intellectual property without explicit written authorization.
- Establish an original robotic visual identity: distinctive armor panelling, head morphology, industrial articulation, and brand palette.

## 4. UI/UX & Visual Direction
- Dark charcoal/black foundations (`#0a0a0c`, `#111317`) with refined metallic finishes and restrained luminous accents (electric blue, warm amber, cyber red).
- Maintain cinematic depth with controlled directional key lights, moody rim lighting, and subtle ambient occlusion.
- Accessible contrast, clear typographical hierarchy, generous negative space, and keyboard-friendly navigation.
- Full support for `prefers-reduced-motion` with clean, instant cross-fades and paused continuous orbital spin.

## 5. Engineering & Quality Workflow
- Always inspect the existing code, dependencies, and layout before making changes.
- Implement in small, verifiable milestones (first ensure the hero is 100% stable before expanding).
- Clean up all event listeners, animation frames, and resize observers upon component unmount.
- Always run `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` before reporting milestones as complete.
